{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edge position ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: ","type":"text"},{"code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traversal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Connectivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShortestPaths","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidentIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes the view’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withIncidenceRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range, O(1). On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the row. On any other base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" binary-search the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"type":"text","text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" finds its place in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them on a base without a faster "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L48"},"externalID":"